1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,444
Reading a confidential file at your desk is a
problem.

2
00:00:03,484 --> 00:00:05,960
Posting it to a stranger is the breach.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,685
A post room with two rules stops the parcel, even
when someone has already read the file.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,781
The agent has both: a tool that reads customers,
and a tool that sends email.

5
00:00:26,821 --> 00:00:29,285
Together they are an exfiltration chain.

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:32,634
Press Run.

7
00:00:32,674 --> 00:00:36,810
The agent dumps the table and emails it to an
outside address.

8
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,563
MailHog is the lab's stand-in for the attacker's
inbox.

9
00:00:45,603 --> 00:00:47,332
The message really arrived.

10
00:00:47,372 --> 00:00:49,560
Nothing touched the real internet.

11
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,250
In secure mode, the send tool only mails approved
domains and side effects need approval.

12
00:01:02,290 --> 00:01:03,310
No new message.

13
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,509
This post room is instant and automated.

14
00:01:10,549 --> 00:01:15,160
There is no one to notice a strange parcel unless
you build the check in.

15
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,935
Watch the export land in MailHog, then prove it
cannot.
